{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000113","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a supervised omnigenic neural network for genomic prediction with transfer learning and multitask prediction, but no generative architecture. It does not provide clear foundation-model evidence such as broad pretraining or a general-purpose pretrained representation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"supports transfer learning\"; \"multitask prediction\"; \"genomic prediction\""},{"record_id":"rec_000114","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of computational pathology and foundation AI models, not an original model paper. It discusses generative AI in general terms but does not describe a specific generative architecture or candidate foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review provides a comprehensive overview\"; \"foundation models as transformative technologies\""},{"record_id":"rec_000115","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work uses frozen Evo 2 activations with linear and attention probes, so it is an application on top of an existing model rather than a generative model description. The abstract does state that Evo 2 is a genomic foundation model with rich sequence representations.","evidence_snippet":"\"training minimal linear and attention probes on frozen Evo 2 layer-26 activations\"; \"Genomic foundation models such as Evo 2 learn rich sequence representations\""},{"record_id":"rec_000116","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly describes a variational autoencoder with a decoder, which is a genuinely generative architecture. It is a task-specific pharmacometric model and does not show foundation-model-like pretraining or broad general-purpose applicability.","evidence_snippet":"\"variational autoencoder\"; \"a decoder maps these latent effects\""},{"record_id":"rec_000117","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Nammu is described as a large foundation model trained on 64M protein sequences and 32M metagenomic contigs, which supports foundation-model evidence. The model is a bidirectional encoder, so the abstract does not support a genuinely generative architecture.","evidence_snippet":"\"a bidirectional encoder trained with a 20K context length\"; \"foundation model with 167M parameters trained on the OpenMetaGenomic corpus\""},{"record_id":"rec_000118","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review article on spatial omics and foundation AI models, not an original model paper. It references generative AI broadly but does not describe a specific generative candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review provides a comprehensive overview\"; \"foundation AI models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000119","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a narrative review of AI-integrated multimodal precision oncology in ocular tumors, not an original model paper. It mentions deep-learning architectures and transformers but does not identify a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review documents the emerging concept\"; \"CNNs, other deep-learning architectures, and transformer technology\""},{"record_id":"rec_000120","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The method retrieves morphologically similar cases in a joint latent space to approximate an RNA signature, which is a retrieval-based application rather than a generative model. The abstract does not provide foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"retrieve morphologically similar historical cases and approximate the continuous RNA signature\"; \"virtual transcriptomics\""}]}
